        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Service it in October.</strong> Every job in this guide is cheap and quick before the season and expensive and slow once parts are sold out and the shop is three weeks deep.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Drain last winter's fuel and refill with treated fresh fuel, change the oil for a cold-weather grade, inspect the belts and cables, set the skid shoes for your surface, and buy a pack of the correct shear pins to keep with the machine.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then run it for fifteen minutes with the auger and drive engaged. That test run is what turns a checklist into confidence, and it is the difference between a machine that works on the morning it matters and a driveway you end up shovelling.
          </p>
